## Customization

### CSS Custom Properties

Override these CSS variables in your theme's CSS:

```css
:root {
  --low-stock-bg: #fef3c7;
  --low-stock-text: #92400e;
  --low-stock-border: #f59e0b;
  
  --critical-stock-bg: #fee2e2;
  --critical-stock-text: #991b1b;
  --critical-stock-border: #ef4444;
  
  --sold-out-bg: #f3f4f6;
  --sold-out-text: #6b7280;
  --sold-out-border: #d1d5db;
}
```

### Theme Editor Integration

Add this to your `config/settings_schema.json` for merchant customization:

```json
{
  "name": "Low Stock Badge",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "low_stock_threshold",
      "label": "Low stock threshold",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 10
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "low_stock_display_mode",
      "label": "Display mode",
      "options": [
        { "value": "exact", "label": "Show exact count" },
        { "value": "text", "label": "Show text only" },
        { "value": "range", "label": "Show range" }
      ],
      "default": "exact"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "low_stock_enabled",
      "label": "Enable low stock badges",
      "default": true
    }
  ]
}
```

Then use in templates:

```liquid
{% if settings.low_stock_enabled %}
  {% render 'inventory-low-stock-badge',
    product: product,
    threshold: settings.low_stock_threshold,
    display_mode: settings.low_stock_display_mode
  %}
{% endif %}
```

